+/* MacSurf port: two-stop linear gradients.
+ *
+ * The core (MacSurf redraw.c) sets fill_type to PLOT_OP_TYPE_LINEAR_GRADIENT
+ * (_H) with fill_colour as the start colour and fill_colour2 as the end
+ * colour. Monkey has no gradient fill primitive, so we band the fill into N
+ * thin solid rectangles. The plot stream records them as N `PLOT RECT`
+ * lines, so a gradient becomes a visible stack of strips (band *count* is
+ * the observable proof; a colour-aware plotter like the Vita frontend would
+ * consume the interpolated per-band colour, which we compute here). Radial
+ * gradients have no bandable axis on this frontend and fall back to a single
+ * solid fill.
+ */
+#define MACMONK_GRAD_BANDS 32
